DETAIL:  ColdFront stores a jsonb value as the text PostgreSQL renders, and DuckDB would store another text for this value.
-- The refusal holds in a WITH entry and in PL/pgSQL.
WITH w AS (UPDATE public.dv SET doc = jsonb_build_object('a', 1) WHERE id = 1) SELECT 1;
ERROR:  coldfront: jsonb column "doc" of "dv" takes only a constant, a parameter or a jsonb column in a cold write
DETAIL:  ColdFront stores a jsonb value as the text PostgreSQL renders, and DuckDB would store another text for this value.
DO $$ BEGIN UPDATE public.dv SET doc = jsonb_build_object('a', 1) WHERE id = 1; END $$;
